   # BlazeDemo Playwright Automation

End-to-end tests for the [BlazeDemo](https://blazedemo.com/) sample travel-booking site, written in TypeScript with Playwright Test and the Page Object Model.

## Coverage

- Select departure and destination cities and search for flights.
- Verify the selected route, available flight rows, and flight selection.
- Complete the passenger and payment form.
- Verify the purchase confirmation, status, amount, and masked card number.
- Capture screenshots, videos, and traces when a test fails.
- Run the type check and end-to-end suite in GitHub Actions on pushes and pull requests.

## Requirements

- Node.js 20 or newer
- npm

## Setup

```bash
npm ci
npx playwright install chromium
```

## Run tests

```bash
# Run the suite headlessly
npm test

# Run with a visible Chromium browser
npm run test:headed

# Open Playwright's interactive test runner
npm run test:ui

# Type-check the TypeScript project
npm run typecheck

# Open the HTML report from the most recent run
npm run report
```

The sample card value in the test is for this demo only. Never use real payment details in automation tests.

## Project structure

```text
Pages/
  ConfirmationPage.ts
  FlightsPage.ts
  Homepage.ts
  PurchasePage.ts
tests/
  booking.spec.ts
playwright.config.ts
tsconfig.json
```

The page classes keep selectors and page actions together; the test spec describes user journeys and verifies their outcomes.
